        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.112,
            0.238,
            0.131
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 115**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.141,
            0.882,
            0.26
          ],
          "content": "**Where should Grumpy place the treasures so that Jumpy cannot reach both the treasures? Check if these pairs are safe: a. 15 and 39 b. 4 and 15 c. 18 and 29 d. 20 and 55**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.269,
            0.469,
            0.287
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Safe pairs are: 4 and 15, 18 and 29."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.324,
            0.233,
            0.342
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page no. 116"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.351,
            0.66,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": "**Q. Which of the following pairs of numbers are co-prime? a. 18 and 35 b. 15 and 37 c. 30 and 415 d. 17 and 69 e. 81 and 18**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.436,
            0.469,
            0.516
          ],
          "content": "Ans. The pairs of co-prime numbers are: a. 18 and 35 b. 15 and 37 d. 17 and 69"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.526,
            0.881,
            0.564
          ],
          "content": "**Q. While playing the ‘idli-vada’ game with different number pairs, Anshu observed something interesting!**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.573,
            0.881,
            0.608
          ],
          "content": "**1. Sometimes the first common multiple was the same as the product of the two numbers.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.617,
            0.881,
            0.654
          ],
          "content": "**2. At other times the first common multiple was less than the product of the two numbers.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.662,
            0.882,
            0.699
          ],
          "content": "**Find examples for each of the above. How is it related to the number pair being co-prime?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.708,
            0.83,
            0.726
          ],
          "content": "Ans. 1. Examples when the first common multiple is the product of the two numbers:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.735,
            0.349,
            0.752
          ],
          "content": "3, 5; 3, 7 and 4, 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.762,
            0.881,
            0.797
          ],
          "content": "2. Examples when the first common multiple is less than the product of the two numbers:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.807,
            0.366,
            0.825
          ],
          "content": "3, 6; 3, 12 and 6, 15"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.834,
            0.882,
            0.869
          ],
          "content": "Whenever the number pair is co-prime the first common multiple is the product of the two numbers."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.493,
